[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Semi-Slav Defence"]
[Variation "Anti-Moscow Variation"]
[ECO "D43"]
[Character "solid,positional"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "pin"]
[Themes "bishop-pair,kingside-fianchetto"]

1. d4 d5 2. c4 c6 3. Nf3 Nf6 4. Nc3 e6 5. Bg5 h6 { Asks the bishop to decide. If it takes on f6, Black gets two bishops; if it retreats, ...dxc4 and ...g5 come into play. }
6. Bxf6 Qxf6 { Retakes with the queen, which now eyes d4 and keeps the pawn structure intact. }
7. e3 ( 7. Qb3 Qd8 { Guards b7 and keeps all options open. } 8. e3 Nd7 ) 7... Nd7 { Develops the last knight and supports ...e5, the central break Black wants. }
8. Bd3 dxc4 { Takes the pawn now that White must spend time recapturing. } 9. Bxc4 g6 { Prepares ...Bg7, which will point at d4 and the long diagonal. } 10. O-O Bg7 { Puts the bishop on the long diagonal, aiming at d4 and the queenside. } *
